diff --git a/docs/source/whats_new.rst b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
index 0a361404c1..181a01dd7b 100644
--- a/docs/source/whats_new.rst
+++ b/docs/source/whats_new.rst
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ Enhancements
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Mainsah2025` subclasses build their EDF file list from the active NEMAR store's ``sourcedata_provenance.json`` (verifying each file against its recorded SHA-256, the same hash ``SHA256SUMS.txt`` lists) when the store holds them, so no ``SHA256SUMS.txt`` request to PhysioNet is made on a store-backed load (:gh:`1316` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - The four Castillos2023 classes take the shared ``4Class-CVEP/`` tree from the NEMAR store (``fill_tree_from_store``) before downloading the shared 0.6 GB ZIP, which is now fetched at most once into the shared cache folder instead of once per class (:gh:`1317` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Rename :class:`moabb.datasets.Lenaig2026` to :class:`moabb.datasets.Gueho2026` (the class used the first author's given name; Crossref 10.1109/BCI69045.2026.11435072 lists Guého, Lénaïg as first author). ``Lenaig2026`` stays as a deprecated alias until 1.9, ``code`` is unchanged so caches/results/NEMAR paths stay valid, and the renamed pair no longer triggers the ``is_abbrev`` warning. Also fix dataset metadata/docstrings found by the W42 class-name audit: PerezBlanco2026 reference [1] title/authors, BNCI2025_002 first author (Kobler), Daly2020 year (2020), Hinss2021 data URL (Zenodo 5055046, the record the loader downloads), Han2026 record title, ErpCore2021_* METADATA (doi/year 2021), and the Ofner2017 'ataset' typo (:gh:`1318` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- :class:`moabb.datasets.Chen2017SingleFlicker`, :class:`moabb.datasets.EPFLP300`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Nguyen2017_V`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Vagaja2023`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Jeong2020`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Stieger2021`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Yi2025`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Yang2025`, :class:`moabb.datasets.Schrag2026Pediatric` and :class:`moabb.datasets.Brandl2020` seed their loader cache from their NEMAR deposits (``nemar_seed_cache``), so a subject mirrored in a deposit loads with no upstream request; EPFLP300 and Schrag2026Pediatric check the seeded tree before downloading their per-subject ZIP, Stieger2021 returns locally seeded session files without listing Figshare, and GuttmannFlury2025 also accepts the double-nested ``S05/S05/...`` tree its deposit holds for subjects 5 and 9 (by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Add ``n_jobs_data`` to all evaluations (default ``1``, unchanged behavior): it is forwarded as ``n_jobs`` to :meth:`~moabb.paradigms.base.BaseParadigm.get_data`, so subjects are loaded in parallel. :meth:`moabb.datasets.base.BaseDataset.get_data` already supported ``n_jobs`` but evaluations never passed it, so loading was always sequential; this matters when reads are latency-bound, e.g. raw EDF files on a network filesystem (:gh:`1250` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Install a ``moabb`` console script (``[project.scripts] moabb = "moabb.run:main"``), so benchmarks run with ``moabb --pipelines=./pipelines/ --evaluations WithinSession`` instead of ``python -m moabb.run ...``; the command-line logic of :mod:`moabb.run` moved into a reusable ``main(argv=None)`` (:gh:`175` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Test MOABB on free-threaded CPython 3.14 (``3.14t``) with an allowed-to-fail CI job that also checks importing MOABB keeps the GIL disabled, and require ``h5py>=3.16.0`` on Python 3.14+, the first h5py release with free-threaded (``cp314t``) wheels (:gh:`829` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
